  "response_text": "The HAL stands for hardware abstraction layer. It sits underneath the operating system, and it provides the interface needed for the operating system to interact with directly with the hardware resources. The layer is \u201cabstract\u201d as it leaves out complex hardware details. This abstraction makes the HAL useful with working with embedded systems, as it generalizes the OS to hardware interface so that the software is not specific to any hardware resources.\\n",
